component CST2010_100L:
    """Coilcraft CST2010-100L SMT current sense transformer, 1:100.
    VERIFIED 2026-07-16: senses up to 47A, usable to 1MHz+ (35kHz tank
    frequency is in-band), -40..+125C, 1500Vrms winding-winding isolation.
    Replaces Triad CST-1005 (5A, 50/60Hz only, 65C max) per BOM audit.
    Footprint hand-built from the Coilcraft datasheet land pattern
    (Document 1100-2); pads 1/2 = primary tabs (Coilcraft 11/12),
    pads 3/4 = secondary (Coilcraft pins 2/4).

    SUPERSEDED 2026-07-25 by CST3015_100E. Its 47A sensed-current limit is
    below the OCP-01 45-55A window, so no burden value could satisfy both
    the spec and the transformer. Retained for reference only -- do not
    instantiate. See docs/hardware/PROTECTION_CHAIN_REVIEW.md."""
    designator_prefix = "T"
    footprint = "temper:CST2010"
    mpn = "CST2010-100L"
    manufacturer = "Coilcraft"
    ratio = 100

    signal P1 ~ pin 1
    signal P2 ~ pin 2
    signal S1 ~ pin 3
    signal S2 ~ pin 4

component CST3015_100E:
    """Coilcraft CST3015-100ED SMT current sense transformer, 1:100.

    Selected 2026-07-25 to resolve the OCP-01 spec/transformer conflict.
    Verified against Coilcraft Document 1608-1 (rev 09/08/25):

      sensed current    88 A        (CST2010-100L: 47 A)
      turns ratio       1:100       unchanged, so the burden math carries over
      frequency         0.78 kHz to >1 MHz; the 35 kHz tank is in band
      volt-time product 638 V-us    vs 35.7 V-us at the trip point -- 18x margin
      DCR               0.0001 ohm primary, 1.54 ohm secondary
      isolation         5000 Vrms 1 min, reinforced, >=8 mm creepage/clearance
      temperature       -40..+125C, AEC-Q200 qualified

    At the 4.99 ohm burden the trip is 50.1 A (worst case 49.4-50.9 A over
    +/-1% parts), leaving 1.73x headroom to the 88 A sensed rating. The
    5000 Vrms reinforced-insulation rating also improves the IEC 60335-1
    position over the CST2010's 1500 Vrms.

    Datasheet note 5: the sensed-current figure is a 40C-rise reference
    point, not an absolute maximum.

    Footprint temper:CST3015 drawn 2026-07-26 from the official Recommended
    Land Pattern (Coilcraft Document 1608-2). Primary pads 9.0 x 4.8mm on
    15.36mm centres; secondary pads 3.0 x 4.6mm on 13.76mm centres. Pad
    numbering matches the datasheet pins directly, so P1/P2/S1/S2 map to
    pads 1/2/3/4 with no remapping.

    This part is physically larger than the CST2010 (body 23.0 x 30.0mm,
    16.6-16.9 g) and will require board re-layout around T1."""
    designator_prefix = "T"
    footprint = "temper:CST3015"
    mpn = "CST3015-100ED"
    manufacturer = "Coilcraft"
    ratio = 100

    signal P1 ~ pin 1
    signal P2 ~ pin 2
    signal S1 ~ pin 3
    signal S2 ~ pin 4

