component Fuse:
    """Bare 5x20mm fuse LINK ONLY -- not a holder+fuse assembly.

    Corrected 2026-07-26 (docs/evidence/2026-07-26-bom-availability-sweep.md,
    Blocker 3 / docs/evidence/2026-07-26-bom-blocker-resolution.md): this
    class's docstring previously claimed "Fuse holder with fuse", and BOM.md
    described F1 as "AC Mains Fuse (holder+fuse)". Neither was true --
    Schurter's 0034.xxxx numbering (this component's `mpn` field, e.g.
    "0034.3129") is its FST fuse-LINK family; fuseholders are a separate
    part family and a separate BOM line. This design had no PCB-mount
    fuseholder anywhere in the 155-part count. See BOM.md Section 1.2 for
    the added fuseholder line (Schurter FUP 0031.2510) that fills that gap.
    The `footprint` below is a placeholder stub, not a real verified
    footprint for either the link or a holder -- see the PCB stub's own
    "(generator stub)" / "Stub for Schurter 0034.3128 fuse holder" comment
    in temper.kicad_pcb.
    """
    designator_prefix = "F"
    footprint = "Fuse:Fuse_Holder_5x20mm"
    current_rating: current
    voltage_rating: voltage
    mpn: str
    signal p1 ~ pin 1
    signal p2 ~ pin 2

