component INA240A1:
    """TI INA240A1 bidirectional, zero-drift current-sense amplifier, G=20 V/V,
    8-pin TSSOP (PW package). MPN INA240A1QPWRQ1 (AEC-Q100 automotive grade).

    VERIFIED 2026-07-26 against two TI datasheets, both fetched and read
    directly (the earlier PDF-fetch timeout + SnapEDA "no pinout data" gap
    that blocked OCP-02 is resolved):
      - INA240 (non-automotive): SBOS662A, July 2016, revised October 2016,
        Section 6 "Pin Configuration and Functions", PW package.
      - INA240-Q1 (this MPN's grade): SBOS808E, August 2016, revised
        December 2021, Section 6, Figure 6-1 "INA240-Q1 PW Package 8-Pin
        TSSOP Top View" + Table 6-1 "Pin Functions".
    Both datasheets give an identical PW (TSSOP-8) pinout:

        1 NC    reserved; non-Q1 says "connect to ground", Q1 says
                "connect to ground or leave floating"
        2 IN+   analog input, connect to supply side of shunt resistor
        3 IN-   analog input, connect to load side of shunt resistor
        4 GND   analog ground
        5 VS    power supply, 2.7 V to 5.5 V
        6 REF2  reference 2 voltage, 0 V to VS
        7 REF1  reference 1 voltage, 0 V to VS
        8 OUT   analog output

    Device body size 3.00 mm x 4.40 mm (TI Device Information table) ->
    KiCad Package_SO.pretty "TSSOP-8_4.4x3mm_P0.65mm" (JEDEC MO-153 Var AA,
    0.65mm pitch), the standard upstream footprint for this body size.

    Common-mode range is -4 V to +80 V (TI datasheet Description section /
    Recommended Operating Conditions), independent of supply voltage. This
    is the reason OCP-02 (docs/hardware/OCP02_DESIGN.md) requires the shunt
    on the LOW side (DC bus return) rather than the high side: a high-side
    placement across the 340V DC bus would put ~340V of common-mode on the
    inputs and destroy the part. See SecondaryOCPComparator in modules.ato
    for a flagged concern about how much common-mode voltage the low-side
    placement actually leaves, given the DC_BUS_RTN topology as built.

    Gain is fixed by grade (TI Device Comparison Table): A1=20 V/V (this
    part), A2=50, A3=100, A4=200 V/V."""
    designator_prefix = "U"
    footprint = "Package_SO:TSSOP-8_4.4x3mm_P0.65mm"
    mpn = "INA240A1QPWRQ1"
    manufacturer = "Texas Instruments"

    # Ratings
    gain = 20  # V/V, fixed (A1 grade)
    v_cm_min = -4V
    v_cm_max = 80V
    v_supply_min = 2.7V
    v_supply_max = 5.5V

    signal NC ~ pin 1
    signal INP ~ pin 2
    signal INN ~ pin 3
    signal GND ~ pin 4
    signal VS ~ pin 5
    signal REF2 ~ pin 6
    signal REF1 ~ pin 7
    signal OUT ~ pin 8

# ==============================================================================
# SAFETY INTERLOCK COMPONENTS
# ==============================================================================

component H11L1:
    """6-pin DIP Schmitt-trigger phototransistor optocoupler (H11LX family).

    Carries the zero-crossing-detect signal across the HV/SELV isolation
    barrier (docs/hardware/SELV_ISOLATION_REDESIGN.md, 2026-07-26): the LED
    (pins 1/2) stays on the HV side, referenced to power_return/dc_bus.gnd_ref;
    the Schmitt-trigger output (pins 4/5/6) is powered from and referenced to
    the SELV domain. This is the part the project's own pre-existing TODO
    (modules.ato, PowerInput ZCD section) already named as the fix.

    VERIFIED 2026-07-26 directly against Everlight's H11LX-series datasheet
    (DPC-0000022 Rev 5, fetched and read): 6-pin DIP, pin 1=Anode, 2=Cathode,
    3=No Connection, 4=Vo, 5=GND, 6=Vcc. Isolation voltage Viso=5000Vrms
    (1-minute AC withstand per the datasheet's own test note -- a dielectric
    strength figure, NOT independently confirmed here as a certified
    reinforced-insulation rating at this design's ~170-340V DC working
    voltage; PCB creepage/clearance across the barrier still needs layout-
    stage verification). UL recognized (File E214129), VDE approved (No.
    132249). Output: Vcc range 3-15V, open-collector, sinks 16mA at
    Vol<=0.4V (needs an external pull-up). LED: Vf ~1.15-1.5V @ 10mA, IF
    abs max 60mA. H11L1 grade (of the L1/L2/L3 family): guaranteed turn-on
    threshold current <=1.6mA -- the tightest/most sensitive of the three,
    and the grade named by the pre-existing TODO.

    MPN below is the bare, second-sourced industry part number -- Vishay,
    onsemi, and Everlight all manufacture pin-compatible H11L1 devices per
    their respective datasheets found during the same search. Confirm the
    exact manufacturer and orderable suffix (through-hole vs SMD, temp
    grade) at procurement; not done here."""
    designator_prefix = "U"
    footprint = "Package_DIP:DIP-6_W7.62mm"
    mpn = "H11L1"
    manufacturer = "Everlight (or pin-compatible Vishay/onsemi H11L1)"

    signal A ~ pin 1    # LED anode -- HV side
    signal K ~ pin 2    # LED cathode -- HV side
    # pin 3: No Connection
    signal VO ~ pin 4   # Open-collector output -- SELV side
    signal GND ~ pin 5  # SELV side ground
    signal VCC ~ pin 6  # SELV side supply, 3-15V

